from a POST urlencoded form or multipart form\nwhen it exists, otherwise it returns an empty string `(\"\")`.","docMarkdown":"PostForm returns the specified key from a POST urlencoded form or multipart form when it exists, otherwise it returns an empty string `(\"\")`.","signature":"func (c *Context) PostForm(key string) (value string)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":610},"examples":[]},{"name":"PostFormArray","doc":"PostFormArray returns a slice of strings for a given form key.\nThe length of the slice depends on the number of params with the given key.","docMarkdown":"PostFormArray returns a slice of strings for a given form key. The length of the slice depends on the number of params with the given key.","signature":"func (c *Context) PostFormArray(key string) (values []string)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":642},"examples":[]},{"name":"PostFormMap","doc":"PostFormMap returns a map for a given form key.","docMarkdown":"PostFormMap returns a map for a given form key.","signature":"func (c *Context) PostFormMap(key string) (dicts map[string]string)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":669},"examples":[]},{"name":"ProtoBuf","doc":"ProtoBuf serializes the given struct as ProtoBuf into the response body.","docMarkdown":"ProtoBuf serializes the given struct as ProtoBuf into the response body.","signature":"func (c *Context) ProtoBuf(code int, obj any)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1298},"examples":[]},{"name":"PureJSON","doc":"PureJSON serializes the given struct as JSON into the response body.\nPureJSON, unlike JSON, does not replace special html characters with their unicode entities.","docMarkdown":"PureJSON serializes the given struct as JSON into the response body. PureJSON, unlike JSON, does not replace special html characters with their unicode entities.","signature":"func (c *Context) PureJSON(code int, obj any)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1271},"examples":[]},{"name":"Query","doc":"Query returns the keyed url query value if it exists,\notherwise it returns an empty string `(\"\")`.\nIt is shortcut for `c.Request.URL.Query().Get(key)`\n\n\t    GET /path?id=1234&name=Manu&value=\n\t\t   c.Query(\"id\") == \"1234\"\n\t\t   c.Query(\"name\") == \"Manu\"\n\t\t   c.Query(\"value\") == \"\"\n\t\t   c.Query(\"wtf\") == \"\"","docMarkdown":"Query returns the keyed url query value if it exists, otherwise it returns an empty string `(\"\")`. It is shortcut for `c.Request.URL.Query().Get(key)`\n\n\t    GET /path?id=1234&name=Manu&value=\n\t\t   c.Query(\"id\") == \"1234\"\n\t\t   c.Query(\"name\") == \"Manu\"\n\t\t   c.Query(\"value\") == \"\"\n\t\t   c.Query(\"wtf\") == \"\"","signature":"func (c *Context) Query(key string) (value string)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":534},"examples":[]},{"name":"QueryArray","doc":"QueryArray returns a slice of strings for a given query key.\nThe length of the slice depends on the number of params with the given key.","docMarkdown":"QueryArray returns a slice of strings for a given query key. The length of the slice depends on the number of params with the given key.","signature":"func (c *Context) QueryArray(key string) (values []string)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":572},"examples":[]},{"name":"QueryMap","doc":"QueryMap returns a map for a given query key.","docMarkdown":"QueryMap returns a map for a given query key.","signature":"func (c *Context) QueryMap(key string) (dicts map[string]string)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":596},"examples":[]},{"name":"Redirect","doc":"Redirect returns an HTTP redirect to the specific location.","docMarkdown":"Redirect returns an HTTP redirect to the specific location.","signature":"func (c *Context) Redirect(code int, location string)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1313},"examples":[]},{"name":"RemoteIP","doc":"RemoteIP parses the IP from Request.RemoteAddr, normalizes and returns the IP (without the port).","docMarkdown":"RemoteIP parses the IP from Request.RemoteAddr, normalizes and returns the IP (without the port).","signature":"func (c *Context) RemoteIP() string","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1049},"examples":[]},{"name":"Render","doc":"Render writes the response headers and calls render.Render to render data.","docMarkdown":"Render writes the response headers and calls render.Render to render data.","signature":"func (c *Context) Render(code int, r render.Render)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1201},"examples":[]},{"name":"SSEvent","doc":"SSEvent writes a Server-Sent Event into the body stream.","docMarkdown":"SSEvent writes a Server-Sent Event into the body stream.","signature":"func (c *Context) SSEvent(name string, message any)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1373},"examples":[]},{"name":"SaveUploadedFile","doc":"SaveUploadedFile uploads the form file to specific dst.\nAn optional perm argument specifies the permission bits used when creating\nthe destination directory. If not provided, the default is 0750. The exact\npermission is enforced only on the destination directory and only when it is\nnewly created by this call; pre-existing directories (e.g. /tmp) are not\nmodified.","docMarkdown":"SaveUploadedFile uploads the form file to specific dst. An optional perm argument specifies the permission bits used when creating the destination directory. If not provided, the default is 0750. The exact permission is enforced only on the destination directory and only when it is newly created by this call; pre-existing directories (e.g. /tmp) are not modified.","signature":"func (c *Context) SaveUploadedFile(file *multipart.FileHeader, dst string, perm ...fs.FileMode) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":733},"examples":[]},{"name":"Scheme","doc":"Scheme returns the HTTP scheme of the request (\"http\" or \"https\").\nWhen running behind reverse proxies or load balancers `Request.URL.Scheme` is usually empty.\nthe original scheme is commonly forwarded via headers such as X-Forwarded-Proto.\nReference:\nhttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/X-Forwarded-Proto","docMarkdown":"Scheme returns the HTTP scheme of the request (\"http\" or \"https\"). When running behind reverse proxies or load balancers `Request.URL.Scheme` is usually empty. the original scheme is commonly forwarded via headers such as X-Forwarded-Proto. Reference: [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/X-Forwarded-Proto](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/X-Forwarded-Proto)","signature":"func (c *Context) Scheme() string","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1077},"examples":[]},{"name":"SecureJSON","doc":"SecureJSON serializes the given struct as Secure JSON into the response body.\nDefault prepends \"while(1);\" to response body if the given struct is array values.\nIt also sets the Content-Type as \"application/json\".","docMarkdown":"SecureJSON serializes the given struct as Secure JSON into the response body. Default prepends \"while(1);\" to response body if the given struct is array values. It also sets the Content-Type as \"application/json\".","signature":"func (c *Context) SecureJSON(code int, obj any)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1241},"examples":[]},{"name":"Set","doc":"Set is used to store a new key/value pair exclusively for this context.\nIt also lazy initializes c.Keys if it was not used previously.","docMarkdown":"Set is used to store a new key/value pair exclusively for this context. It also lazy initializes c.Keys if it was not used previously.","signature":"func (c *Context) Set(key any, value any)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":285},"examples":[]},{"name":"SetAccepted","doc":"SetAccepted sets Accept header data.","docMarkdown":"SetAccepted sets Accept header data.","signature":"func (c *Context) SetAccepted(formats ...string)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1485},"examples":[]},{"name":"SetCookie","doc":"SetCookie adds a Set-Cookie header to the ResponseWriter's headers.\nThe provided cookie must have a valid Name. Invalid cookies may be\nsilently dropped.","docMarkdown":"SetCookie adds a Set-Cookie header to the ResponseWriter's headers. The provided cookie must have a valid Name. Invalid cookies may be silently dropped.","signature":"func (c *Context) SetCookie(name, value string, maxAge int, path, domain string, secure, httpOnly bool)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1158},"examples":[]},{"name":"SetCookieData","doc":"SetCookieData adds a Set-Cookie header to the ResponseWriter's headers.\nIt accepts a pointer to http.Cookie structure for more flexibility in setting cookie attributes.\nThe provided cookie must have a valid Name. Invalid cookies may be silently dropped.","docMarkdown":"SetCookieData adds a Set-Cookie header to the ResponseWriter's headers. It accepts a pointer to http.Cookie structure for more flexibility in setting cookie attributes. The provided cookie must have a valid Name. Invalid cookies may be silently dropped.","signature":"func (c *Context) SetCookieData(cookie *http.Cookie)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1177},"examples":[]},{"name":"SetSameSite","doc":"SetSameSite with cookie","docMarkdown":"SetSameSite with cookie","signature":"func (c *Context) SetSameSite(samesite http.SameSite)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1151},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBind","doc":"ShouldBind checks the Method and Content-Type to select a binding engine automatically,\nDepending on the \"Content-Type\" header different bindings are used, for example:\n\n\t\"application/json\" --> JSON binding\n\t\"application/xml\"  --> XML binding\n\nIt parses the request's body based on the Content-Type (e.g., JSON or XML).\nIt decodes the payload into the struct specified as a pointer.\nLike c.Bind() but this method does not set the response status code to 400 or abort if input is not valid.","docMarkdown":"ShouldBind checks the Method and Content-Type to select a binding engine automatically, Depending on the \"Content-Type\" header different bindings are used, for example:\n\n\t\"application/json\" --> JSON binding\n\t\"application/xml\"  --> XML binding\n\nIt parses the request's body based on the Content-Type (e.g., JSON or XML). It decodes the payload into the struct specified as a pointer. Like c.Bind() but this method does not set the response status code to 400 or abort if input is not valid.","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBind(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":860},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindBodyWith","doc":"ShouldBindBodyWith is similar with ShouldBindWith, but it stores the request\nbody into the context, and reuse when it is called again.\n\nNOTE: This method reads the body before binding. So you should use\nShouldBindWith for better performance if you need to call only once.","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindBodyWith is similar with ShouldBindWith, but it stores the request body into the context, and reuse when it is called again.\n\nNOTE: This method reads the body before binding. So you should use ShouldBindWith for better performance if you need to call only once.","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindBodyWith(obj any, bb binding.BindingBody) (err error)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":950},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindBodyWithJSON","doc":"ShouldBindBodyWithJSON is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindBodyWith(obj, binding.JSON).","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindBodyWithJSON is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindBodyWith(obj, binding.JSON).","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindBodyWithJSON(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":968},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindBodyWithPlain","doc":"ShouldBindBodyWithPlain is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindBodyWith(obj, binding.Plain).","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindBodyWithPlain is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindBodyWith(obj, binding.Plain).","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindBodyWithPlain(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":988},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindBodyWithTOML","doc":"ShouldBindBodyWithTOML is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindBodyWith(obj, binding.TOML).","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindBodyWithTOML is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindBodyWith(obj, binding.TOML).","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindBodyWithTOML(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":983},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindBodyWithXML","doc":"ShouldBindBodyWithXML is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindBodyWith(obj, binding.XML).","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindBodyWithXML is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindBodyWith(obj, binding.XML).","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindBodyWithXML(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":973},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindBodyWithYAML","doc":"ShouldBindBodyWithYAML is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindBodyWith(obj, binding.YAML).","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindBodyWithYAML is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindBodyWith(obj, binding.YAML).","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindBodyWithYAML(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":978},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindHeader","doc":"ShouldBindHeader is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.Header).\nIt works like ShouldBindJSON but binds values from HTTP headers.","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindHeader is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.Header). It works like ShouldBindJSON but binds values from HTTP headers.","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindHeader(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":925},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindJSON","doc":"ShouldBindJSON is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.JSON).\n\nExample:\n\n\tPOST /user\n\tContent-Type: application/json\n\n\tRequest Body:\n\t{\n\t\t\"name\": \"Manu\",\n\t\t\"age\": 20\n\t}\n\n\ttype User struct {\n\t\tName string `json:\"name\"`\n\t\tAge  int    `json:\"age\"`\n\t}\n\n\tvar user User\n\tif err := c.ShouldBindJSON(&user); err != nil {\n\t\tc.JSON(http.StatusBadRequest, gin.H{\"error\": err.Error()})\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tc.JSON(http.StatusOK, user)","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindJSON is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.JSON).\n\nExample:\n\n\tPOST /user\n\tContent-Type: application/json\n\n\tRequest Body:\n\t{\n\t\t\"name\": \"Manu\",\n\t\t\"age\": 20\n\t}\n\n\ttype User struct {\n\t\tName string `json:\"name\"`\n\t\tAge  int    `json:\"age\"`\n\t}\n\n\tvar user User\n\tif err := c.ShouldBindJSON(&user); err != nil {\n\t\tc.JSON(http.StatusBadRequest, gin.H{\"error\": err.Error()})\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tc.JSON(http.StatusOK, user)","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindJSON(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":889},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindPlain","doc":"ShouldBindPlain is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.Plain).\nIt works like ShouldBindJSON but binds plain text data from the request body.","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindPlain is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.Plain). It works like ShouldBindJSON but binds plain text data from the request body.","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindPlain(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":919},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindQuery","doc":"ShouldBindQuery is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.Query).\nIt works like ShouldBindJSON but binds query parameters from the URL.","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindQuery is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.Query). It works like ShouldBindJSON but binds query parameters from the URL.","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindQuery(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":901},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindTOML","doc":"ShouldBindTOML is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.TOML).\nIt works like ShouldBindJSON but binds the request body as TOML data.","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindTOML is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.TOML). It works like ShouldBindJSON but binds the request body as TOML data.","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindTOML(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":913},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindUri","doc":"ShouldBindUri binds the passed struct pointer using the specified binding engine.\nIt works like ShouldBindJSON but binds parameters from the URI.","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindUri binds the passed struct pointer using the specified binding engine. It works like ShouldBindJSON but binds parameters from the URI.","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindUri(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":931},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindWith","doc":"ShouldBindWith binds the passed struct pointer using the specified binding engine.\nSee the binding package.","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindWith binds the passed struct pointer using the specified binding engine. See the binding package.","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindWith(obj any, b binding.Binding) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":941},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindXML","doc":"ShouldBindXML is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.XML).\nIt works like ShouldBindJSON but binds the request body as XML data.","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindXML is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.XML). It works like ShouldBindJSON but binds the request body as XML data.","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindXML(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":895},"examples":[]},{"name":"ShouldBindYAML","doc":"ShouldBindYAML is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.YAML).\nIt works like ShouldBindJSON but binds the request body as YAML data.","docMarkdown":"ShouldBindYAML is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.YAML). It works like ShouldBindJSON but binds the request body as YAML data.","signature":"func (c *Context) ShouldBindYAML(obj any) error","position":{"file":"context.go","line":907},"examples":[]},{"name":"Status","doc":"Status sets the HTTP response code.","docMarkdown":"Status sets the HTTP response code.","signature":"func (c *Context) Status(code int)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1122},"examples":[]},{"name":"Stream","doc":"Stream sends a streaming response and returns a boolean\nindicates \"Is client disconnected in middle of stream\"","docMarkdown":"Stream sends a streaming response and returns a boolean indicates \"Is client disconnected in middle of stream\"","signature":"func (c *Context) Stream(step func(w io.Writer) bool) bool","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1382},"examples":[]},{"name":"String","doc":"String writes the given string into the response body.","docMarkdown":"String writes the given string into the response body.","signature":"func (c *Context) String(code int, format string, values ...any)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1308},"examples":[]},{"name":"TOML","doc":"TOML serializes the given struct as TOML into the response body.","docMarkdown":"TOML serializes the given struct as TOML into the response body.","signature":"func (c *Context) TOML(code int, obj any)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1293},"examples":[]},{"name":"Value","doc":"Value returns the value associated with this context for key, or nil\nif no value is associated with key. Successive calls to Value with\nthe same key returns the same result.","docMarkdown":"Value returns the value associated with this context for key, or nil if no value is associated with key. Successive calls to Value with the same key returns the same result.","signature":"func (c *Context) Value(key any) any","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1527},"examples":[]},{"name":"XML","doc":"XML serializes the given struct as XML into the response body.\nIt also sets the Content-Type as \"application/xml\".","docMarkdown":"XML serializes the given struct as XML into the response body. It also sets the Content-Type as \"application/xml\".","signature":"func (c *Context) XML(code int, obj any)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1277},"examples":[]},{"name":"YAML","doc":"YAML serializes the given struct as YAML into the response body.","docMarkdown":"YAML serializes the given struct as YAML into the response body.","signature":"func (c *Context) YAML(code int, obj any)","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1288},"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"name":"ContextKeyType","doc":"","declaration":"type ContextKeyType int","kind":"defined","position":{"file":"context.go","line":52},"fields":[],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"Engine","doc":"Engine is the framework's instance, it contains the muxer, middleware and configuration settings.\nCreate an instance of Engine, by using New() or Default()","docMarkdown":"Engine is the framework's instance, it contains the muxer, middleware and configuration settings. Create an instance of Engine, by using New() or Default()","declaration":"type Engine struct {\n\tRouterGroup\n\n\t// RedirectTrailingSlash enables automatic redirection if the current route can't be matched but a\n\t// handler for the path with (without) the trailing slash exists.\n\t// For example if /foo/ is requested but a route only exists for /foo, the\n\t// client is redirected to /foo with http status code 301 for GET requests\n\t// and 307 for all other request methods.\n\tRedirectTrailingSlash bool\n\n\t// RedirectFixedPath if enabled, the router tries to fix the current request path, if no\n\t// handle is registered for it.\n\t// First superfluous path elements like ../ or // are removed.\n\t// Afterwards the router does a case-insensitive lookup of the cleaned path.\n\t// If a handle can be found for this route, the router makes a redirection\n\t// to the corrected path with status code 301 for GET requests and 307 for\n\t// all other request methods.\n\t// For example /FOO and /..//Foo could be redirected to /foo.\n\t// RedirectTrailingSlash is independent of this option.\n\tRedirectFixedPath bool\n\n\t// HandleMethodNotAllowed if enabled, the router checks if another method is allowed for the\n\t// current route, if the current request can not be routed.\n\t// If this is the case, the request is answered with 'Method Not Allowed'\n\t// and HTTP status code 405.\n\t// If no other Method is allowed, the request is delegated to the NotFound\n\t// handler.\n\tHandleMethodNotAllowed bool\n\n\t// ForwardedByClientIP if enabled, client IP will be parsed from the request's headers that\n\t// match those stored at `(*gin.Engine).RemoteIPHeaders`. If no IP was\n\t// fetched, it falls back to the IP obtained from\n\t// `(*gin.Context).Request.RemoteAddr`.\n\tForwardedByClientIP bool\n\n\t// AppEngine was deprecated.\n\t// Deprecated: USE `TrustedPlatform` WITH VALUE `gin.PlatformGoogleAppEngine` INSTEAD\n\t// #726 #755 If enabled, it will trust some headers starting with\n\t// 'X-AppEngine...' for better integration with that PaaS.\n\tAppEngine bool\n\n\t// UseRawPath if enabled, the url.RawPath will be used to find parameters.\n\t// The RawPath is only a hint, EscapedPath() should be use instead. (https://pkg.go.dev/net/url@master#URL)\n\t// Only use RawPath if you know what you are doing.\n\tUseRawPath bool\n\n\t// UseEscapedPath if enable, the url.EscapedPath() will be used to find parameters\n\t// It overrides UseRawPath\n\tUseEscapedPath bool\n\n\t// UnescapePathValues if true, the path value will be unescaped.\n\t// If UseRawPath and UseEscapedPath are false (by default), the UnescapePathValues effectively is true,\n\t// as url.Path gonna be used, which is already unescaped.\n\tUnescapePathValues bool\n\n\t// RemoveExtraSlash a parameter can be parsed from the URL even with extra slashes.\n\t// See the PR #1817 and issue #1644\n\tRemoveExtraSlash bool\n\n\t// RemoteIPHeaders list of headers used to obtain the client IP when\n\t// `(*gin.Engine).ForwardedByClientIP` is `true` and\n\t// `(*gin.Context).Request.RemoteAddr` is matched by at least one of the\n\t// network origins of list defined by `(*gin.Engine).SetTrustedProxies()`.\n\tRemoteIPHeaders []string\n\n\t// TrustedPlatform if set to a constant of value gin.Platform*, trusts the headers set by\n\t// that platform, for example to determine the client IP\n\tTrustedPlatform string\n\n\t// MaxMultipartMemory value of 'maxMemory' param that is given to http.Request's ParseMultipartForm\n\t// method call.\n\tMaxMultipartMemory int64\n\n\t// ReadHeaderTimeout is the maximum duration allowed for reading the request\n\t// headers by the http.Server created through Run, RunTLS and RunListener.\n\t// If zero or negative, a default of 10 seconds is used. Set to a positive\n\t// value to customize, or use a custom http.Server directly to disable it.\n\tReadHeaderTimeout time.Duration\n\n\t// UseH2C enable h2c support.\n\tUseH2C bool\n\n\t// ContextWithFallback enable fallback Context.Deadline(), Context.Done(), Context.Err() and Context.Value() when Context.Request.Context() is not nil.\n\tContextWithFallback bool\n\n\tHTMLRender render.HTMLRender\n\tFuncMap    template.FuncMap\n\t// contains filtered or unexported fields\n}","kind":"struct","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":99},"fields":[{"name":"RouterGroup","doc":"","type":"RouterGroup","embedded":true},{"name":"RedirectTrailingSlash","doc":"RedirectTrailingSlash enables automatic redirection if the current route can't be matched but a\nhandler for the path with (without) the trailing slash exists.\nFor example if /foo/ is requested but a route only exists for /foo, the\nclient is redirected to /foo with http status code 301 for GET requests\nand 307 for all other request methods.","docMarkdown":"RedirectTrailingSlash enables automatic redirection if the current route can't be matched but a handler for the path with (without) the trailing slash exists. For example if /foo/ is requested but a route only exists for /foo, the client is redirected to /foo with http status code 301 for GET requests and 307 for all other request methods.","type":"bool"},{"name":"RedirectFixedPath","doc":"RedirectFixedPath if enabled, the router tries to fix the current request path, if no\nhandle is registered for it.\nFirst superfluous path elements like ../ or // are removed.\nAfterwards the router does a case-insensitive lookup of the cleaned path.\nIf a handle can be found for this route, the router makes a redirection\nto the corrected path with status code 301 for GET requests and 307 for\nall other request methods.\nFor example /FOO and /..//Foo could be redirected to /foo.\nRedirectTrailingSlash is independent of this option.","docMarkdown":"RedirectFixedPath if enabled, the router tries to fix the current request path, if no handle is registered for it. First superfluous path elements like ../ or // are removed. Afterwards the router does a case-insensitive lookup of the cleaned path. If a handle can be found for this route, the router makes a redirection to the corrected path with status code 301 for GET requests and 307 for all other request methods. For example /FOO and /..//Foo could be redirected to /foo. RedirectTrailingSlash is independent of this option.","type":"bool"},{"name":"HandleMethodNotAllowed","doc":"HandleMethodNotAllowed if enabled, the router checks if another method is allowed for the\ncurrent route, if the current request can not be routed.\nIf this is the case, the request is answered with 'Method Not Allowed'\nand HTTP status code 405.\nIf no other Method is allowed, the request is delegated to the NotFound\nhandler.","docMarkdown":"HandleMethodNotAllowed if enabled, the router checks if another method is allowed for the current route, if the current request can not be routed. If this is the case, the request is answered with 'Method Not Allowed' and HTTP status code 405. If no other Method is allowed, the request is delegated to the NotFound handler.","type":"bool"},{"name":"ForwardedByClientIP","doc":"ForwardedByClientIP if enabled, client IP will be parsed from the request's headers that\nmatch those stored at `(*gin.Engine).RemoteIPHeaders`. If no IP was\nfetched, it falls back to the IP obtained from\n`(*gin.Context).Request.RemoteAddr`.","docMarkdown":"ForwardedByClientIP if enabled, client IP will be parsed from the request's headers that match those stored at `(*gin.Engine).RemoteIPHeaders`. If no IP was fetched, it falls back to the IP obtained from `(*gin.Context).Request.RemoteAddr`.","type":"bool"},{"name":"AppEngine","doc":"AppEngine was deprecated.\nDeprecated: USE `TrustedPlatform` WITH VALUE `gin.PlatformGoogleAppEngine` INSTEAD\n#726 #755 If enabled, it will trust some headers starting with\n'X-AppEngine...' for better integration with that PaaS.","docMarkdown":"AppEngine was deprecated. Deprecated: USE `TrustedPlatform` WITH VALUE `gin.PlatformGoogleAppEngine` INSTEAD #726 #755 If enabled, it will trust some headers starting with 'X-AppEngine...' for better integration with that PaaS.","type":"bool"},{"name":"UseRawPath","doc":"UseRawPath if enabled, the url.RawPath will be used to find parameters.\nThe RawPath is only a hint, EscapedPath() should be use instead. (https://pkg.go.dev/net/url@master#URL)\nOnly use RawPath if you know what you are doing.","docMarkdown":"UseRawPath if enabled, the url.RawPath will be used to find parameters. The RawPath is only a hint, EscapedPath() should be use instead. ([https://pkg.go.dev/net/url@master#URL](https://pkg.go.dev/net/url@master#URL)) Only use RawPath if you know what you are doing.","type":"bool"},{"name":"UseEscapedPath","doc":"UseEscapedPath if enable, the url.EscapedPath() will be used to find parameters\nIt overrides UseRawPath","docMarkdown":"UseEscapedPath if enable, the url.EscapedPath() will be used to find parameters It overrides UseRawPath","type":"bool"},{"name":"UnescapePathValues","doc":"UnescapePathValues if true, the path value will be unescaped.\nIf UseRawPath and UseEscapedPath are false (by default), the UnescapePathValues effectively is true,\nas url.Path gonna be used, which is already unescaped.","docMarkdown":"UnescapePathValues if true, the path value will be unescaped. If UseRawPath and UseEscapedPath are false (by default), the UnescapePathValues effectively is true, as url.Path gonna be used, which is already unescaped.","type":"bool"},{"name":"RemoveExtraSlash","doc":"RemoveExtraSlash a parameter can be parsed from the URL even with extra slashes.\nSee the PR #1817 and issue #1644","docMarkdown":"RemoveExtraSlash a parameter can be parsed from the URL even with extra slashes. See the PR #1817 and issue #1644","type":"bool"},{"name":"RemoteIPHeaders","doc":"RemoteIPHeaders list of headers used to obtain the client IP when\n`(*gin.Engine).ForwardedByClientIP` is `true` and\n`(*gin.Context).Request.RemoteAddr` is matched by at least one of the\nnetwork origins of list defined by `(*gin.Engine).SetTrustedProxies()`.","docMarkdown":"RemoteIPHeaders list of headers used to obtain the client IP when `(*gin.Engine).ForwardedByClientIP` is `true` and `(*gin.Context).Request.RemoteAddr` is matched by at least one of the network origins of list defined by `(*gin.Engine).SetTrustedProxies()`.","type":"[]string"},{"name":"TrustedPlatform","doc":"TrustedPlatform if set to a constant of value gin.Platform*, trusts the headers set by\nthat platform, for example to determine the client IP","docMarkdown":"TrustedPlatform if set to a constant of value gin.Platform\\*, trusts the headers set by that platform, for example to determine the client IP","type":"string"},{"name":"MaxMultipartMemory","doc":"MaxMultipartMemory value of 'maxMemory' param that is given to http.Request's ParseMultipartForm\nmethod call.","docMarkdown":"MaxMultipartMemory value of 'maxMemory' param that is given to http.Request's ParseMultipartForm method call.","type":"int64"},{"name":"ReadHeaderTimeout","doc":"ReadHeaderTimeout is the maximum duration allowed for reading the request\nheaders by the http.Server created through Run, RunTLS and RunListener.\nIf zero or negative, a default of 10 seconds is used. Set to a positive\nvalue to customize, or use a custom http.Server directly to disable it.","docMarkdown":"ReadHeaderTimeout is the maximum duration allowed for reading the request headers by the http.Server created through Run, RunTLS and RunListener. If zero or negative, a default of 10 seconds is used. Set to a positive value to customize, or use a custom http.Server directly to disable it.","type":"time.Duration"},{"name":"UseH2C","doc":"UseH2C enable h2c support.","docMarkdown":"UseH2C enable h2c support.","type":"bool"},{"name":"ContextWithFallback","doc":"ContextWithFallback enable fallback Context.Deadline(), Context.Done(), Context.Err() and Context.Value() when Context.Request.Context() is not nil.","docMarkdown":"ContextWithFallback enable fallback Context.Deadline(), Context.Done(), Context.Err() and Context.Value() when Context.Request.Context() is not nil.","type":"bool"},{"name":"HTMLRender","doc":"","type":"render.HTMLRender"},{"name":"FuncMap","doc":"","type":"template.FuncMap"}],"methods":[{"name":"Delims","doc":"Delims sets template left and right delims and returns an Engine instance.","docMarkdown":"Delims sets template left and right delims and returns an Engine instance.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) Delims(left, right string) *Engine","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":282},"examples":[]},{"name":"HandleContext","doc":"HandleContext re-enters a context that has been rewritten.\nThis can be done by setting c.Request.URL.Path to your new target.\nDisclaimer: You can loop yourself to deal with this, use wisely.","docMarkdown":"HandleContext re-enters a context that has been rewritten. This can be done by setting c.Request.URL.Path to your new target. Disclaimer: You can loop yourself to deal with this, use wisely.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) HandleContext(c *Context)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":709},"examples":[]},{"name":"Handler","doc":"","signature":"func (engine *Engine) Handler() http.Handler","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":257},"examples":[]},{"name":"LoadHTMLFS","doc":"LoadHTMLFS loads an http.FileSystem and a slice of patterns\nand associates the result with HTML renderer.","docMarkdown":"LoadHTMLFS loads an http.FileSystem and a slice of patterns and associates the result with HTML renderer.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) LoadHTMLFS(fs http.FileSystem, patterns ...string)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":323},"examples":[]},{"name":"LoadHTMLFiles","doc":"LoadHTMLFiles loads a slice of HTML files\nand associates the result with HTML renderer.","docMarkdown":"LoadHTMLFiles loads a slice of HTML files and associates the result with HTML renderer.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) LoadHTMLFiles(files ...string)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":311},"examples":[]},{"name":"LoadHTMLGlob","doc":"LoadHTMLGlob loads HTML files identified by glob pattern\nand associates the result with HTML renderer.","docMarkdown":"LoadHTMLGlob loads HTML files identified by glob pattern and associates the result with HTML renderer.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) LoadHTMLGlob(pattern string)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":295},"examples":[]},{"name":"NoMethod","doc":"NoMethod sets the handlers called when Engine.HandleMethodNotAllowed = true.","docMarkdown":"NoMethod sets the handlers called when Engine.HandleMethodNotAllowed = true.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) NoMethod(handlers ...HandlerFunc)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":355},"examples":[]},{"name":"NoRoute","doc":"NoRoute adds handlers for NoRoute. It returns a 404 code by default.","docMarkdown":"NoRoute adds handlers for NoRoute. It returns a 404 code by default.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) NoRoute(handlers ...HandlerFunc)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":349},"examples":[]},{"name":"Routes","doc":"Routes returns a slice of registered routes, including some useful information, such as:\nthe http method, path, and the handler name.","docMarkdown":"Routes returns a slice of registered routes, including some useful information, such as: the http method, path, and the handler name.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) Routes() (routes RoutesInfo)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":413},"examples":[]},{"name":"Run","doc":"Run attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests.\nIt is a shortcut for http.ListenAndServe(addr, router)\nNote: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.\nThe created http.Server is configured with a default ReadHeaderTimeout of 10 seconds\n(configurable via Engine.ReadHeaderTimeout) to mitigate slowloris attacks.\nFor full control over timeouts, create a custom http.Server and use ServeHTTP.","docMarkdown":"Run attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests. It is a shortcut for http.ListenAndServe(addr, router) Note: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens. The created http.Server is configured with a default ReadHeaderTimeout of 10 seconds (configurable via Engine.ReadHeaderTimeout) to mitigate slowloris attacks. For full control over timeouts, create a custom http.Server and use ServeHTTP.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) Run(addr ...string) (err error)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":566},"examples":[]},{"name":"RunFd","doc":"RunFd attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests\nthrough the specified file descriptor.\nNote: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","docMarkdown":"RunFd attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests through the specified file descriptor. Note: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) RunFd(fd int) (err error)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":635},"examples":[]},{"name":"RunListener","doc":"RunListener attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests\nthrough the specified net.Listener","docMarkdown":"RunListener attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests through the specified net.Listener","signature":"func (engine *Engine) RunListener(listener net.Listener) (err error)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":673},"examples":[]},{"name":"RunQUIC","doc":"RunQUIC attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving QUIC requests.\nIt is a shortcut for http3.ListenAndServeQUIC(addr, certFile, keyFile, router)\nNote: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","docMarkdown":"RunQUIC attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving QUIC requests. It is a shortcut for http3.ListenAndServeQUIC(addr, certFile, keyFile, router) Note: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) RunQUIC(addr, certFile, keyFile string) (err error)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":658},"examples":[]},{"name":"RunTLS","doc":"RunTLS attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTPS (secure) requests.\nIt is a shortcut for http.ListenAndServeTLS(addr, certFile, keyFile, router)\nNote: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","docMarkdown":"RunTLS attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTPS (secure) requests. It is a shortcut for http.ListenAndServeTLS(addr, certFile, keyFile, router) Note: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) RunTLS(addr, certFile, keyFile string) (err error)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":588},"examples":[]},{"name":"RunUnix","doc":"RunUnix attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests\nthrough the specified unix socket (i.e. a file).\nNote: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","docMarkdown":"RunUnix attaches the router to a http.Server and starts listening and serving HTTP requests through the specified unix socket (i.e. a file). Note: this method will block the calling goroutine indefinitely unless an error happens.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) RunUnix(file string) (err error)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":609},"examples":[]},{"name":"SecureJsonPrefix","doc":"SecureJsonPrefix sets the secureJSONPrefix used in Context.SecureJSON.","docMarkdown":"SecureJsonPrefix sets the secureJSONPrefix used in Context.SecureJSON.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) SecureJsonPrefix(prefix string) *Engine","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":288},"examples":[]},{"name":"ServeHTTP","doc":"ServeHTTP conforms to the http.Handler interface.","docMarkdown":"ServeHTTP conforms to the http.Handler interface.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) ServeHTTP(w http.ResponseWriter, req *http.Request)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":691},"examples":[]},{"name":"SetFuncMap","doc":"SetFuncMap sets the FuncMap used for template.FuncMap.","docMarkdown":"SetFuncMap sets the FuncMap used for template.FuncMap.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) SetFuncMap(funcMap template.FuncMap)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":344},"examples":[]},{"name":"SetHTMLTemplate","doc":"SetHTMLTemplate associate a template with HTML renderer.","docMarkdown":"SetHTMLTemplate associate a template with HTML renderer.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) SetHTMLTemplate(templ *template.Template)","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":335},"examples":[]},{"name":"SetTrustedProxies","doc":"SetTrustedProxies set a list of network origins (IPv4 addresses,\nIPv4 CIDRs, IPv6 addresses or IPv6 CIDRs) from which to trust\nrequest's headers that contain alternative client IP when\n`(*gin.Engine).ForwardedByClientIP` is `true`. `TrustedProxies`\nfeature is enabled by default, and it also trusts all proxies\nby default. If you want to disable this feature, use\nEngine.SetTrustedProxies(nil), then Context.ClientIP() will\nreturn the remote address directly.","docMarkdown":"SetTrustedProxies set a list of network origins (IPv4 addresses, IPv4 CIDRs, IPv6 addresses or IPv6 CIDRs) from which to trust request's headers that contain alternative client IP when `(*gin.Engine).ForwardedByClientIP` is `true`. `TrustedProxies` feature is enabled by default, and it also trusts all proxies by default. If you want to disable this feature, use Engine.SetTrustedProxies(nil), then Context.ClientIP() will return the remote address directly.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) SetTrustedProxies(trustedProxies []string) error","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":474},"examples":[]},{"name":"Use","doc":"Use attaches a global middleware to the router. i.e. the middleware attached through Use() will be\nincluded in the handlers chain for every single request. Even 404, 405, static files...\nFor example, this is the right place for a logger or error management middleware.","docMarkdown":"Use attaches a global middleware to the router. i.e. the middleware attached through Use() will be included in the handlers chain for every single request. Even 404, 405, static files... For example, this is the right place for a logger or error management middleware.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) Use(middleware ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":363},"examples":[]},{"name":"With","doc":"With returns an Engine with the configuration set in the OptionFunc.","docMarkdown":"With returns an Engine with the configuration set in the OptionFunc.","signature":"func (engine *Engine) With(opts ...OptionFunc) *Engine","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":371},"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"name":"Error","doc":"Error represents a error's specification.","docMarkdown":"Error represents a error's specification.","declaration":"type Error struct {\n\tErr  error\n\tType ErrorType\n\tMeta any\n}","kind":"struct","position":{"file":"errors.go","line":32},"fields":[{"name":"Err","doc":"","type":"error"},{"name":"Type","doc":"","type":"ErrorType"},{"name":"Meta","doc":"","type":"any"}],"methods":[{"name":"Error","doc":"Error implements the error interface.","docMarkdown":"Error implements the error interface.","signature":"func (msg Error) Error() string","position":{"file":"errors.go","line":82},"examples":[]},{"name":"IsType","doc":"IsType judges one error.","docMarkdown":"IsType judges one error.","signature":"func (msg *Error) IsType(flags ErrorType) bool","position":{"file":"errors.go","line":87},"examples":[]},{"name":"JSON","doc":"JSON creates a properly formatted JSON","docMarkdown":"JSON creates a properly formatted JSON","signature":"func (msg *Error) JSON() any","position":{"file":"errors.go","line":55},"examples":[]},{"name":"MarshalJSON","doc":"MarshalJSON implements the json.Marshaller interface.","docMarkdown":"MarshalJSON implements the json.Marshaller interface.","signature":"func (msg *Error) MarshalJSON() ([]byte, error)","position":{"file":"errors.go","line":77},"examples":[]},{"name":"SetMeta","doc":"SetMeta sets the error's meta data.","docMarkdown":"SetMeta sets the error's meta data.","signature":"func (msg *Error) SetMeta(data any) *Error","position":{"file":"errors.go","line":49},"examples":[]},{"name":"SetType","doc":"SetType sets the error's type.","docMarkdown":"SetType sets the error's type.","signature":"func (msg *Error) SetType(flags ErrorType) *Error","position":{"file":"errors.go","line":43},"examples":[]},{"name":"Unwrap","doc":"Unwrap returns the wrapped error, to allow interoperability with errors.Is(), errors.As() and errors.Unwrap()","docMarkdown":"Unwrap returns the wrapped error, to allow interoperability with errors.Is(), errors.As() and errors.Unwrap()","signature":"func (msg Error) Unwrap() error","position":{"file":"errors.go","line":92},"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"name":"ErrorType","doc":"ErrorType is an unsigned 64-bit error code as defined in the gin spec.","docMarkdown":"ErrorType is an unsigned 64-bit error code as defined in the gin spec.","declaration":"type ErrorType uint64","kind":"defined","position":{"file":"errors.go","line":16},"fields":[],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"H","doc":"H is a shortcut for map[string]any","docMarkdown":"H is a shortcut for map\\[string]any","declaration":"type H map[string]any","kind":"defined","position":{"file":"utils.go","line":62},"fields":[],"methods":[{"name":"MarshalXML","doc":"MarshalXML allows type H to be used with xml.Marshal.","docMarkdown":"MarshalXML allows type H to be used with xml.Marshal.","signature":"func (h H) MarshalXML(e *xml.Encoder, start xml.StartElement) error","position":{"file":"utils.go","line":65},"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"name":"HandlerFunc","doc":"HandlerFunc defines the handler used by gin middleware as return value.","docMarkdown":"HandlerFunc defines the handler used by gin middleware as return value.","declaration":"type HandlerFunc func(*Context)","kind":"defined","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":58},"fields":[],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"HandlersChain","doc":"HandlersChain defines a HandlerFunc slice.","docMarkdown":"HandlersChain defines a HandlerFunc slice.","declaration":"type HandlersChain []HandlerFunc","kind":"defined","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":64},"fields":[],"methods":[{"name":"Last","doc":"Last returns the last handler in the chain. i.e. the last handler is the main one.","docMarkdown":"Last returns the last handler in the chain. i.e. the last handler is the main one.","signature":"func (c HandlersChain) Last() HandlerFunc","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":67},"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"name":"IQueryRoutes","doc":"IQueryRoutes defines the router handle interface for the HTTP QUERY method.\n\nIt is deliberately kept out of IRoutes: adding a method to IRoutes would\nbreak every type outside of Gin that implements it, such as test doubles and\nwrappers. Type assert when you only hold an IRoutes value:\n\n\tif q, ok := routes.(gin.IQueryRoutes); ok {\n\t\tq.QUERY(\"/search\", handler)\n\t}\n\n*gin.RouterGroup and *gin.Engine satisfy this interface, so the assertion is\nonly needed when the concrete type has been erased.","docMarkdown":"IQueryRoutes defines the router handle interface for the HTTP QUERY method.\n\nIt is deliberately kept out of IRoutes: adding a method to IRoutes would break every type outside of Gin that implements it, such as test doubles and wrappers. Type assert when you only hold an IRoutes value:\n\n\tif q, ok := routes.(gin.IQueryRoutes); ok {\n\t\tq.QUERY(\"/search\", handler)\n\t}\n\n\\*gin.RouterGroup and \\*gin.Engine satisfy this interface, so the assertion is only needed when the concrete type has been erased.","declaration":"type IQueryRoutes interface {\n\tQUERY(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes\n}","kind":"interface","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":70},"fields":[{"name":"QUERY","doc":"","type":"func(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"IRouter","doc":"IRouter defines all router handle interface includes single and group router.","docMarkdown":"IRouter defines all router handle interface includes single and group router.","declaration":"type IRouter interface {\n\tIRoutes\n\tGroup(string, ...HandlerFunc) *RouterGroup\n}","kind":"interface","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":32},"fields":[{"name":"IRoutes","doc":"","type":"IRoutes","embedded":true},{"name":"Group","doc":"","type":"func(string, ...HandlerFunc) *RouterGroup"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"IRoutes","doc":"IRoutes defines all router handle interface.","docMarkdown":"IRoutes defines all router handle interface.","declaration":"type IRoutes interface {\n\tUse(...HandlerFunc) IRoutes\n\n\tHandle(string, string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes\n\tAny(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes\n\tGET(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes\n\tPOST(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes\n\tDELETE(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes\n\tPATCH(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes\n\tPUT(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes\n\tOPTIONS(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes\n\tHEAD(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes\n\tMatch([]string, string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes\n\n\tStaticFile(string, string) IRoutes\n\tStaticFileFS(string, string, http.FileSystem) IRoutes\n\tStatic(string, string) IRoutes\n\tStaticFS(string, http.FileSystem) IRoutes\n}","kind":"interface","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":38},"fields":[{"name":"Use","doc":"","type":"func(...HandlerFunc) IRoutes"},{"name":"Handle","doc":"","type":"func(string, string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes"},{"name":"Any","doc":"","type":"func(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes"},{"name":"GET","doc":"","type":"func(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes"},{"name":"POST","doc":"","type":"func(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes"},{"name":"DELETE","doc":"","type":"func(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes"},{"name":"PATCH","doc":"","type":"func(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes"},{"name":"PUT","doc":"","type":"func(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes"},{"name":"OPTIONS","doc":"","type":"func(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes"},{"name":"HEAD","doc":"","type":"func(string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes"},{"name":"Match","doc":"","type":"func([]string, string, ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes"},{"name":"StaticFile","doc":"","type":"func(string, string) IRoutes"},{"name":"StaticFileFS","doc":"","type":"func(string, string, http.FileSystem) IRoutes"},{"name":"Static","doc":"","type":"func(string, string) IRoutes"},{"name":"StaticFS","doc":"","type":"func(string, http.FileSystem) IRoutes"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"LogFormatter","doc":"LogFormatter gives the signature of the formatter function passed to LoggerWithFormatter","docMarkdown":"LogFormatter gives the signature of the formatter function passed to LoggerWithFormatter","declaration":"type LogFormatter func(params LogFormatterParams) string","kind":"defined","position":{"file":"logger.go","line":65},"fields":[],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"LogFormatterParams","doc":"LogFormatterParams is the structure any formatter will be handed when time to log comes","docMarkdown":"LogFormatterParams is the structure any formatter will be handed when time to log comes","declaration":"type LogFormatterParams struct {\n\tRequest *http.Request\n\n\t// TimeStamp shows the time after the server returns a response.\n\tTimeStamp time.Time\n\t// StatusCode is HTTP response code.\n\tStatusCode int\n\t// Latency is how much time the server cost to process a certain request.\n\tLatency time.Duration\n\t// ClientIP equals Context's ClientIP method.\n\tClientIP string\n\t// Method is the HTTP method given to the request.\n\tMethod string\n\t// Path is a path the client requests.\n\tPath string\n\t// ErrorMessage is set if error has occurred in processing the request.\n\tErrorMessage string\n\n\t// BodySize is the size of the Response Body\n\tBodySize int\n\t// Keys are the keys set on the request's context.\n\tKeys map[any]any\n\t// contains filtered or unexported fields\n}","kind":"struct","position":{"file":"logger.go","line":68},"fields":[{"name":"Request","doc":"","type":"*http.Request"},{"name":"TimeStamp","doc":"TimeStamp shows the time after the server returns a response.","docMarkdown":"TimeStamp shows the time after the server returns a response.","type":"time.Time"},{"name":"StatusCode","doc":"StatusCode is HTTP response code.","docMarkdown":"StatusCode is HTTP response code.","type":"int"},{"name":"Latency","doc":"Latency is how much time the server cost to process a certain request.","docMarkdown":"Latency is how much time the server cost to process a certain request.","type":"time.Duration"},{"name":"ClientIP","doc":"ClientIP equals Context's ClientIP method.","docMarkdown":"ClientIP equals Context's ClientIP method.","type":"string"},{"name":"Method","doc":"Method is the HTTP method given to the request.","docMarkdown":"Method is the HTTP method given to the request.","type":"string"},{"name":"Path","doc":"Path is a path the client requests.","docMarkdown":"Path is a path the client requests.","type":"string"},{"name":"ErrorMessage","doc":"ErrorMessage is set if error has occurred in processing the request.","docMarkdown":"ErrorMessage is set if error has occurred in processing the request.","type":"string"},{"name":"BodySize","doc":"BodySize is the size of the Response Body","docMarkdown":"BodySize is the size of the Response Body","type":"int"},{"name":"Keys","doc":"Keys are the keys set on the request's context.","docMarkdown":"Keys are the keys set on the request's context.","type":"map[any]any"}],"methods":[{"name":"IsOutputColor","doc":"IsOutputColor indicates whether can colors be outputted to the log.","docMarkdown":"IsOutputColor indicates whether can colors be outputted to the log.","signature":"func (p *LogFormatterParams) IsOutputColor() bool","position":{"file":"logger.go","line":162},"examples":[]},{"name":"LatencyColor","doc":"LatencyColor is the ANSI color for latency","docMarkdown":"LatencyColor is the ANSI color for latency","signature":"func (p *LogFormatterParams) LatencyColor() string","position":{"file":"logger.go","line":112},"examples":[]},{"name":"MethodColor","doc":"MethodColor is the ANSI color for appropriately logging http method to a terminal.","docMarkdown":"MethodColor is the ANSI color for appropriately logging http method to a terminal.","signature":"func (p *LogFormatterParams) MethodColor() string","position":{"file":"logger.go","line":133},"examples":[]},{"name":"ResetColor","doc":"ResetColor resets all escape attributes.","docMarkdown":"ResetColor resets all escape attributes.","signature":"func (p *LogFormatterParams) ResetColor() string","position":{"file":"logger.go","line":157},"examples":[]},{"name":"StatusCodeColor","doc":"StatusCodeColor is the ANSI color for appropriately logging http status code to a terminal.","docMarkdown":"StatusCodeColor is the ANSI color for appropriately logging http status code to a terminal.","signature":"func (p *LogFormatterParams) StatusCodeColor() string","position":{"file":"logger.go","line":94},"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"name":"LoggerConfig","doc":"LoggerConfig defines the config for Logger middleware.","docMarkdown":"LoggerConfig defines the config for Logger middleware.","declaration":"type LoggerConfig struct {\n\t// Optional. Default value is gin.defaultLogFormatter\n\tFormatter LogFormatter\n\n\t// Output is a writer where logs are written.\n\t// Optional. Default value is gin.DefaultWriter.\n\tOutput io.Writer\n\n\t// SkipPaths is a URL path array which logs are not written.\n\t// Optional.\n\tSkipPaths []string\n\n\t// SkipQueryString indicates that query strings should not be written\n\t// for cases such as when API keys are passed via query strings.\n\t// Optional. Default value is false.\n\tSkipQueryString bool\n\n\t// Skip is a Skipper that indicates which logs should not be written.\n\t// Optional.\n\tSkip Skipper\n}","kind":"struct","position":{"file":"logger.go","line":39},"fields":[{"name":"Formatter","doc":"Optional. Default value is gin.defaultLogFormatter","docMarkdown":"Optional. Default value is gin.defaultLogFormatter","type":"LogFormatter"},{"name":"Output","doc":"Output is a writer where logs are written.\nOptional. Default value is gin.DefaultWriter.","docMarkdown":"Output is a writer where logs are written. Optional. Default value is gin.DefaultWriter.","type":"io.Writer"},{"name":"SkipPaths","doc":"SkipPaths is a URL path array which logs are not written.\nOptional.","docMarkdown":"SkipPaths is a URL path array which logs are not written. Optional.","type":"[]string"},{"name":"SkipQueryString","doc":"SkipQueryString indicates that query strings should not be written\nfor cases such as when API keys are passed via query strings.\nOptional. Default value is false.","docMarkdown":"SkipQueryString indicates that query strings should not be written for cases such as when API keys are passed via query strings. Optional. Default value is false.","type":"bool"},{"name":"Skip","doc":"Skip is a Skipper that indicates which logs should not be written.\nOptional.","docMarkdown":"Skip is a Skipper that indicates which logs should not be written. Optional.","type":"Skipper"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"Negotiate","doc":"Negotiate contains all negotiations data.","docMarkdown":"Negotiate contains all negotiations data.","declaration":"type Negotiate struct {\n\tOffered      []string\n\tHTMLName     string\n\tHTMLData     any\n\tJSONData     any\n\tXMLData      any\n\tYAMLData     any\n\tData         any\n\tTOMLData     any\n\tPROTOBUFData any\n\tBSONData     any\n}","kind":"struct","position":{"file":"context.go","line":1404},"fields":[{"name":"Offered","doc":"","type":"[]string"},{"name":"HTMLName","doc":"","type":"string"},{"name":"HTMLData","doc":"","type":"any"},{"name":"JSONData","doc":"","type":"any"},{"name":"XMLData","doc":"","type":"any"},{"name":"YAMLData","doc":"","type":"any"},{"name":"Data","doc":"","type":"any"},{"name":"TOMLData","doc":"","type":"any"},{"name":"PROTOBUFData","doc":"","type":"any"},{"name":"BSONData","doc":"","type":"any"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"OnlyFilesFS","doc":"OnlyFilesFS implements an http.FileSystem without `Readdir` functionality.","docMarkdown":"OnlyFilesFS implements an http.FileSystem without `Readdir` functionality.","declaration":"type OnlyFilesFS struct {\n\tFileSystem http.FileSystem\n}","kind":"struct","position":{"file":"fs.go","line":13},"fields":[{"name":"FileSystem","doc":"","type":"http.FileSystem"}],"methods":[{"name":"Open","doc":"Open passes `Open` to the upstream implementation without `Readdir` functionality.","docMarkdown":"Open passes `Open` to the upstream implementation without `Readdir` functionality.","signature":"func (o OnlyFilesFS) Open(name string) (http.File, error)","position":{"file":"fs.go","line":18},"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"name":"OptionFunc","doc":"OptionFunc defines the function to change the default configuration","docMarkdown":"OptionFunc defines the function to change the default configuration","declaration":"type OptionFunc func(*Engine)","kind":"defined","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":61},"fields":[],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"Param","doc":"Param is a single URL parameter, consisting of a key and a value.","docMarkdown":"Param is a single URL parameter, consisting of a key and a value.","declaration":"type Param struct {\n\tKey   string\n\tValue string\n}","kind":"struct","position":{"file":"tree.go","line":17},"fields":[{"name":"Key","doc":"","type":"string"},{"name":"Value","doc":"","type":"string"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"Params","doc":"Params is a Param-slice, as returned by the router.\nThe slice is ordered, the first URL parameter is also the first slice value.\nIt is therefore safe to read values by the index.","docMarkdown":"Params is a Param-slice, as returned by the router. The slice is ordered, the first URL parameter is also the first slice value. It is therefore safe to read values by the index.","declaration":"type Params []Param","kind":"defined","position":{"file":"tree.go","line":25},"fields":[],"methods":[{"name":"ByName","doc":"ByName returns the value of the first Param which key matches the given name.\nIf no matching Param is found, an empty string is returned.","docMarkdown":"ByName returns the value of the first Param which key matches the given name. If no matching Param is found, an empty string is returned.","signature":"func (ps Params) ByName(name string) (va string)","position":{"file":"tree.go","line":40},"examples":[]},{"name":"Get","doc":"Get returns the value of the first Param which key matches the given name and a boolean true.\nIf no matching Param is found, an empty string is returned and a boolean false .","docMarkdown":"Get returns the value of the first Param which key matches the given name and a boolean true. If no matching Param is found, an empty string is returned and a boolean false .","signature":"func (ps Params) Get(name string) (string, bool)","position":{"file":"tree.go","line":29},"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"name":"RecoveryFunc","doc":"RecoveryFunc defines the function passable to CustomRecovery.","docMarkdown":"RecoveryFunc defines the function passable to CustomRecovery.","declaration":"type RecoveryFunc func(c *Context, err any)","kind":"defined","position":{"file":"recovery.go","line":32},"fields":[],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"ResponseWriter","doc":"ResponseWriter ...","docMarkdown":"ResponseWriter ...","declaration":"type ResponseWriter interface {\n\thttp.ResponseWriter\n\thttp.Hijacker\n\thttp.Flusher\n\thttp.CloseNotifier\n\n\t// Status returns the HTTP response status code of the current request.\n\tStatus() int\n\n\t// Size returns the number of bytes already written into the response http body.\n\t// See Written()\n\tSize() int\n\n\t// WriteString writes the string into the response body.\n\tWriteString(string) (int, error)\n\n\t// Written returns true if the response body was already written.\n\tWritten() bool\n\n\t// WriteHeaderNow forces to write the http header (status code + headers).\n\tWriteHeaderNow()\n\n\t// Pusher get the http.Pusher for server push\n\tPusher() http.Pusher\n}","kind":"interface","position":{"file":"response_writer.go","line":23},"fields":[{"name":"http.ResponseWriter","doc":"","type":"http.ResponseWriter","embedded":true},{"name":"http.Hijacker","doc":"","type":"http.Hijacker","embedded":true},{"name":"http.Flusher","doc":"","type":"http.Flusher","embedded":true},{"name":"http.CloseNotifier","doc":"","type":"http.CloseNotifier","embedded":true},{"name":"Status","doc":"Status returns the HTTP response status code of the current request.","docMarkdown":"Status returns the HTTP response status code of the current request.","type":"func() int"},{"name":"Size","doc":"Size returns the number of bytes already written into the response http body.\nSee Written()","docMarkdown":"Size returns the number of bytes already written into the response http body. See Written()","type":"func() int"},{"name":"WriteString","doc":"WriteString writes the string into the response body.","docMarkdown":"WriteString writes the string into the response body.","type":"func(string) (int, error)"},{"name":"Written","doc":"Written returns true if the response body was already written.","docMarkdown":"Written returns true if the response body was already written.","type":"func() bool"},{"name":"WriteHeaderNow","doc":"WriteHeaderNow forces to write the http header (status code + headers).","docMarkdown":"WriteHeaderNow forces to write the http header (status code + headers).","type":"func()"},{"name":"Pusher","doc":"Pusher get the http.Pusher for server push","docMarkdown":"Pusher get the http.Pusher for server push","type":"func() http.Pusher"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"RouteInfo","doc":"RouteInfo represents a request route's specification which contains method and path and its handler.","docMarkdown":"RouteInfo represents a request route's specification which contains method and path and its handler.","declaration":"type RouteInfo struct {\n\tMethod      string\n\tPath        string\n\tHandler     string\n\tHandlerFunc HandlerFunc\n}","kind":"struct","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":75},"fields":[{"name":"Method","doc":"","type":"string"},{"name":"Path","doc":"","type":"string"},{"name":"Handler","doc":"","type":"string"},{"name":"HandlerFunc","doc":"","type":"HandlerFunc"}],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"RouterGroup","doc":"RouterGroup is used internally to configure router, a RouterGroup is associated with\na prefix and an array of handlers (middleware).","docMarkdown":"RouterGroup is used internally to configure router, a RouterGroup is associated with a prefix and an array of handlers (middleware).","declaration":"type RouterGroup struct {\n\tHandlers HandlersChain\n\t// contains filtered or unexported fields\n}","kind":"struct","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":76},"fields":[{"name":"Handlers","doc":"","type":"HandlersChain"}],"methods":[{"name":"Any","doc":"Any registers a route that matches all the HTTP methods.\nGET, POST, PUT, PATCH, HEAD, OPTIONS, DELETE, CONNECT, TRACE, QUERY.","docMarkdown":"Any registers a route that matches all the HTTP methods. GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, HEAD, OPTIONS, DELETE, CONNECT, TRACE, QUERY.","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) Any(relativePath string, handlers ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":182},"examples":[]},{"name":"BasePath","doc":"BasePath returns the base path of router group.\nFor example, if v := router.Group(\"/rest/n/v1/api\"), v.BasePath() is \"/rest/n/v1/api\".","docMarkdown":"BasePath returns the base path of router group. For example, if v := router.Group(\"/rest/n/v1/api\"), v.BasePath() is \"/rest/n/v1/api\".","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) BasePath() string","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":106},"examples":[]},{"name":"DELETE","doc":"DELETE is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"DELETE\", path, handlers).","docMarkdown":"DELETE is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"DELETE\", path, handlers).","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) DELETE(relativePath string, handlers ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":147},"examples":[]},{"name":"GET","doc":"GET is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"GET\", path, handlers).","docMarkdown":"GET is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"GET\", path, handlers).","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) GET(relativePath string, handlers ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":142},"examples":[]},{"name":"Group","doc":"Group creates a new router group. You should add all the routes that have common middlewares or the same path prefix.\nFor example, all the routes that use a common middleware for authorization could be grouped.","docMarkdown":"Group creates a new router group. You should add all the routes that have common middlewares or the same path prefix. For example, all the routes that use a common middleware for authorization could be grouped.","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) Group(relativePath string, handlers ...HandlerFunc) *RouterGroup","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":96},"examples":[]},{"name":"HEAD","doc":"HEAD is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"HEAD\", path, handlers).","docMarkdown":"HEAD is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"HEAD\", path, handlers).","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) HEAD(relativePath string, handlers ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":167},"examples":[]},{"name":"Handle","doc":"Handle registers a new request handle and middleware with the given path and method.\nThe last handler should be the real handler, the other ones should be middleware that can and should be shared among different routes.\nSee the example code in GitHub.\n\nFor GET, POST, PUT, PATCH and DELETE requests the respective shortcut\nfunctions can be used.\n\nThis function is intended for bulk loading and to allow the usage of less\nfrequently used, non-standardized or custom methods (e.g. for internal\ncommunication with a proxy).\n\nIt panics if httpMethod is not a valid HTTP method (uppercase ASCII letters only).","docMarkdown":"Handle registers a new request handle and middleware with the given path and method. The last handler should be the real handler, the other ones should be middleware that can and should be shared among different routes. See the example code in GitHub.\n\nFor GET, POST, PUT, PATCH and DELETE requests the respective shortcut functions can be used.\n\nThis function is intended for bulk loading and to allow the usage of less frequently used, non-standardized or custom methods (e.g. for internal communication with a proxy).\n\nIt panics if httpMethod is not a valid HTTP method (uppercase ASCII letters only).","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) Handle(httpMethod, relativePath string, handlers ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":129},"examples":[]},{"name":"Match","doc":"Match registers a route that matches the specified methods that you declared.","docMarkdown":"Match registers a route that matches the specified methods that you declared.","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) Match(methods []string, relativePath string, handlers ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":191},"examples":[]},{"name":"OPTIONS","doc":"OPTIONS is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"OPTIONS\", path, handlers).","docMarkdown":"OPTIONS is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"OPTIONS\", path, handlers).","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) OPTIONS(relativePath string, handlers ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":162},"examples":[]},{"name":"PATCH","doc":"PATCH is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"PATCH\", path, handlers).","docMarkdown":"PATCH is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"PATCH\", path, handlers).","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) PATCH(relativePath string, handlers ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":152},"examples":[]},{"name":"POST","doc":"POST is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"POST\", path, handlers).","docMarkdown":"POST is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"POST\", path, handlers).","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) POST(relativePath string, handlers ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":137},"examples":[]},{"name":"PUT","doc":"PUT is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"PUT\", path, handlers).","docMarkdown":"PUT is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"PUT\", path, handlers).","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) PUT(relativePath string, handlers ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":157},"examples":[]},{"name":"QUERY","doc":"QUERY is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"QUERY\", path, handlers).\n\nQUERY is the safe and idempotent method defined by RFC 10008 that carries its\nquery in the request body. The body is read like any other body, for example\nwith c.ShouldBindJSON.","docMarkdown":"QUERY is a shortcut for router.Handle(\"QUERY\", path, handlers).\n\nQUERY is the safe and idempotent method defined by RFC 10008 that carries its query in the request body. The body is read like any other body, for example with c.ShouldBindJSON.","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) QUERY(relativePath string, handlers ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":176},"examples":[]},{"name":"Static","doc":"Static serves files from the given file system root.\nInternally a http.FileServer is used, therefore http.NotFound is used instead\nof the Router's NotFound handler.\nTo use the operating system's file system implementation,\nuse :\n\n\trouter.Static(\"/static\", \"/var/www\")","docMarkdown":"Static serves files from the given file system root. Internally a http.FileServer is used, therefore http.NotFound is used instead of the Router's NotFound handler. To use the operating system's file system implementation, use :\n\n\trouter.Static(\"/static\", \"/var/www\")","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) Static(relativePath, root string) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":232},"examples":[]},{"name":"StaticFS","doc":"StaticFS works just like `Static()` but a custom `http.FileSystem` can be used instead.\nGin by default uses: gin.Dir()\nIt panics if relativePath contains URL parameters (: or *).","docMarkdown":"StaticFS works just like `Static()` but a custom `http.FileSystem` can be used instead. Gin by default uses: gin.Dir() It panics if relativePath contains URL parameters (: or \\*).","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) StaticFS(relativePath string, fs http.FileSystem) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":239},"examples":[]},{"name":"StaticFile","doc":"StaticFile registers a single route in order to serve a single file of the local filesystem.\nrouter.StaticFile(\"favicon.ico\", \"./resources/favicon.ico\")","docMarkdown":"StaticFile registers a single route in order to serve a single file of the local filesystem. router.StaticFile(\"favicon.ico\", \"./resources/favicon.ico\")","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) StaticFile(relativePath, filepath string) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":201},"examples":[]},{"name":"StaticFileFS","doc":"StaticFileFS works just like `StaticFile` but a custom `http.FileSystem` can be used instead.\nrouter.StaticFileFS(\"favicon.ico\", \"./resources/favicon.ico\", Dir{\".\", false})\nGin by default uses: gin.Dir()","docMarkdown":"StaticFileFS works just like `StaticFile` but a custom `http.FileSystem` can be used instead. router.StaticFileFS(\"favicon.ico\", \"./resources/favicon.ico\", Dir{\".\", false}) Gin by default uses: gin.Dir()","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) StaticFileFS(relativePath, filepath string, fs http.FileSystem) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":210},"examples":[]},{"name":"Use","doc":"Use adds middleware to the group, see example code in GitHub.","docMarkdown":"Use adds middleware to the group, see example code in GitHub.","signature":"func (group *RouterGroup) Use(middleware ...HandlerFunc) IRoutes","position":{"file":"routergroup.go","line":89},"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"name":"RoutesInfo","doc":"RoutesInfo defines a RouteInfo slice.","docMarkdown":"RoutesInfo defines a RouteInfo slice.","declaration":"type RoutesInfo []RouteInfo","kind":"defined","position":{"file":"gin.go","line":83},"fields":[],"methods":[],"examples":[]},{"name":"Skipper","doc":"Skipper is a function to skip logs based on provided Context","docMarkdown":"Skipper is a function to skip logs based on provided Context","declaration":"type Skipper func(c *Context) bool","kind":"defined","position":{"file":"logger.go","line":62},"fields":[],"methods":[],"examples":[]}],"examples":[]},{"importPath":"github.com/gin-gonic/gin/binding","name":"binding","synopsis":"","doc":"","dir":"binding","files":["binding/binding.go","binding/bson.go","binding/default_validator.go","binding/form.go","binding/form_mapping.go","binding/header.go","binding/json.go","binding/msgpack.go","binding/multipart_form_mapping.go","binding/plain.go","binding/protobuf.go","binding/query.go","binding/toml.go","binding/uri.go","binding/xml.go","binding/yaml.go"],"consts":[{"name":"MIMEJSON","doc":"Content-Type MIME of the most common data formats.","docMarkdown":"Content-Type MIME of the most common data formats.","declaration":"const (\n\tMIMEJSON              = \"application/json\"\n\tMIMEHTML              = \"text/html\"\n\tMIMEXML               = \"application/xml\"\n\tMIMEXML2              = \"text/xml\"\n\tMIMEPlain             = \"text/plain\"\n\tMIMEPOSTForm          = \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\"\n\tMIMEMultipartPOSTForm = \"multipart/form-data\"\n\tMIMEPROTOBUF          = \"application/x-protobuf\"\n\tMIMEMSGPACK           = \"application/x-msgpack\"\n\tMIMEMSGPACK2          = \"application/msgpack\"\n\tMIMEYAML              = \"application/x-yaml\"\n\tMIMEYAML2             = \"application/yaml\"\n\tMIMETOML              = \"application/toml\"\n\tMIMEBSON              = \"application/bson\"\n)","position":{"file":"binding/binding.go","line":13}